       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n**Ibuprofen 1600 mg PO four times daily is 6,400 mg/day.** The usual maximum oral ibuprofen dose is 3,200 mg/day, which is double the limit of 1,600 mg/day for a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function. The single dose of 1,600 mg is also above the usual 800 mg maximum per dose. Doses this high raise the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nCould you confirm the intended regimen? Some possibilities:\n- **400 mg PO QID** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO TID** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO QID** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,600 mg PO BID** (3,200 mg/day, if the 1,600 mg dose was intentional)\n\nIf the 6,400 mg/day regimen is intentional, please tell me why, and I can enter it with a note documenting the rationale. Once you confirm, I'll enter the order."
      }
